-Abstract
-This paper evaluates image preprocessing for YOLOv8n-based ball arrangement inspection. Five-fold cross-validation separates near-duplicate groups
-across 500 images, and key conditions are repeated with three seeds. Agreement with annotation-derived OK/NG decisions is distinguished from strict
-accuracy, which requires detecting every annotated ball without extra detections. Under Gaussian noise with a standard deviation of 80, Gaussian blur
-improves strict accuracy from 72.00% to 94.13%. With noise of 40 and only 25% of the training data, CLAHE improves it from 39.80% to 55.27%. These
-findings indicate condition-dependent benefits. Independent inspection labels and external evaluation across acquisition conditions remain necessary.
-Key words
-YOLOv8n, ball arrangement inspection, image preprocessing, strict accuracy, cross-validation
