-Abstract
-This study compares ten single filters and five ordered combinations
-for YOLOv8n ball detection, motivated by uncertain image
-characteristics in deployment. Group-separated five-fold cross-validation
-uses 500 images. Gamma 0.3 yields the highest clean-image mAP50-95
-among single filters at 96.70%, whereas Gaussian Blur (max) performs
-best under strong Gaussian noise. No combination exceeds its better
-component in mAP. The strict-accuracy gain of Invert+CLAHE in one
-seed is not retained across repeated runs. Neither arbitrary filtering nor
-composition consistently improves detection. Filter selection must
-therefore account for the input condition and evaluation metric.
-Key words: YOLOv8n, image preprocessing, filter combination, object 
-detection
